
Brain Tester READ_ME file

This Java 11 Swing app was designed and created in the open-source Eclipse IDE using WindowBuilder
and a shared H2 Database.

CLASSES, TABLES, METHODS, AND INSTRUCTIONS ON THEIR USE AND DEPLOYMENT:

OVERIEW: The Brain Tester application is where the student takes exams created in the Brain Builder. 
After providing last and first names, an exam must first be selected from the dropdown menu by clicking
the arrow. Then, click 'Begin Exam' whereupon the question and answer fields populate the data fields
along with exam and question number, title, topic, etc. Currently, five (5) multiple choice questions
are provided, with only one selection answer permitted. 

Before beginning, a dialog prompts the student user with respect to the preferred question evaluation timing. 
The user may choose to evaluate each question upon its completion. Once graded/evaluated, the correct/incorrect 
answers are displayed immediately. Or, the user may choose to evaluate and grade all questions 
one time at the conclusion of the exam. Click Evaluate, Next, or Previous, and then Finish when done. 
After exams are finished and graded the user may review them at a later time (see the REVIEWING GRADED EXAMS section below).

