EVALUATE (Grade) QUESTIONS ----------------------------------------------

Many people (author included) prefer to have each question evaluated and graded immediately. An
answer is selected, 'Evaluate' is clicked, and pass/fail is displayed along with the correct answers
including detailed explanations and other useful and relevant information. Some people, on the other hand,
prefer to have all exams graded in a batch at one time at the end after all questions have been answered. 
Then, they wade through that batch one by one if they wish to review the material. 
Clicking 'Begin Exam' initially prompts the user to make that choice.

Assuming the user chooses to evaluate and grade each question immediately, the first code of
consequence in the actionPerformed() method of the 'Evaluate' button (section) captures  the student's 
radio button answer selection. First, a Boolean list (radioButtonSelections) is initialized with five (5) false values,
and then a series of if statements captures the specific selection and sets that particular list index to true. And it is this 
list of the student's choice that is compared to the professor's original list of correct 
answers (theProfsCorrectAnswers). If these two ArrayLists are equal the student passes, if not, then it's a fail. 
After a radio button selection is made in the 'Evaluate' button section the
professor's correct answers are retrieved (theProfsCorrectAnswers = listOfQuestionsSER.get(qNumber).getProfsCorrectAnswers();

IMMEDIATE EVALUATION - If the student user chose immediate evaluation the student's radioButtonSelections ArrayList 
is tested for equality with theProfsCorrectAnswers, and if equal the anon object's setPassFail("pass") is set to "pass."
Then, the indexOfTrueSelected is run through a series of switch/case statements and correct answers are 
displayed accordingly - the results are immediate. With each evaluation the listOfQuestionsSER is populated with 
graded/evaluated questions.

NON-IMMEDIATE OR BULK EVALUATION - Those users who choose to evaluate their questions one time in bulk at the conclusion
of the exam (in the else statement) merely add the button selection list radioButtonSelections 
to gradeOnceListOfListsSER, a global variable of type ArrayList<ArrayList<Boolean>>; a list of a list 
of Booleans (gradeOnceListOfListsSER.add(radioButtonSelections). Bulk evaluation has not yet employed 
a listOfQuestionsSER as in the immediate evaluation procedure. That comes next 
after all questions have been answered (evaluated) and the 'Finish' button is clicked.

